<div style="background-color: #e0f2f7; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-align: center;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # I'm Outside. I'm Happy! – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; font-size: 1.1em; margin-top: 10px;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Grade:</b> 3rd Grade (CEFR: A1.1)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Scenario:</b> I Can Connect with Nature!</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Theme:</b> I'm Outside. I'm Happy!</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Specific Objective:</b> Reading: Summarize a text using a graphic organizer. Reading: Follow written instructions for making or doing something simple. Phonemic Awareness: Blend spoken phonemes to form one-syllable or two-syllable words if these words have been previously encountered.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can summarize a short text about nature using a graphic organizer by organizing key nature terms (e.g., "sun," "tree," and "bird" under the heading "Nature"). Can follow simple instructions from a nature-themed text (e.g., "Draw a leaf."). Can blend spoken phonemes to form one-syllable or two-syllable words, such as blending /s/ /ʌ/ /n/ sounds to form the word "sun" when the words have been previously encountered.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays flashcards of nature items (e.g., sun, tree, flower, bird, leaf, grass, river) previously introduced in Lesson 1. The teacher says, "Look! What can you see?" and encourages students to call out the words. The teacher holds up a flashcard, says the word, and has students repeat. For example, "Sun. Repeat: Sun."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Modeling:</b> The teacher models the pronunciation of key vocabulary and phonemic awareness. The teacher points to a flashcard of the "sun" and slowly says the sounds: "/s/ /ʌ/ /n/ - sun." Students listen. The teacher repeats, "Sun. I can see the sun!" The teacher also models /k/ in "can" and /s/ in "sun". For "flower," the teacher models "/f/ /l/ /ɑʊ/ /ɚ/ - flower."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of the vocabulary. For example: "Is the sun big or small?" (Expected answer: Big!). "Can a bird fly?" (Expected answer: Yes!). "Is a tree green?" (Expected answer: Yes!).</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Material:</b> A short illustrated descriptive text about a visit to a park, titled "My Happy Park Day." The text describes a child enjoying nature, using target vocabulary (tree, grass, flower, bird, sun, river) and grammar (Present simple: "I'm happy," Prepositions of place: "I'm outside," Can/Can't: "I can relax."). It also includes a simple instruction to draw something.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Expressing connection with nature: Talking about sensory observations and experiences in nature (e.g., "I hear the birds."). Locating people and things: Identifying locations in nature (e.g., "I am near the big tree.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Text Example:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"My Happy Park Day"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"I'm outside today! I'm at the park. I'm happy! The sun is bright in the sky. I can see a big green tree. I'm under the tree. The grass is green. I can see a beautiful flower. I hear the birds sing. I can relax here. There is a small river. I like this nature spot. Draw a yellow sun!"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> Teacher asks, "Where is the child?" (Expected answer: At the park/outside.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> The teacher reads simple statements, and students say "True" or "False" based on the text.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "The sun is blue." (False)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "The tree is big." (True)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. "I can hear the dogs." (False)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Reading comprehension, identifying key vocabulary, understanding simple grammar (Can/Can't, Prepositions of place, Present simple). Pronunciation practice of /k/ and /s/, blending phonemes.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Controlled Practice (Matching):</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with sentences from "My Happy Park Day" (or similar short sentences) and a word bank (e.g., tree, bird, sun, flower, grass, river). Students read each sentence and fill in the missing word.</li>
                        <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; margin-top: 4px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "I can see a big green ______." (tree)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "I hear the _______ sing." (birds)</li>
                        </ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Semi-controlled Practice (Sentence Completion):</b> The teacher displays incomplete sentences related to nature on the board. Students read the sentences and complete them with an appropriate nature word from a provided list or picture prompts. Focus on words that can be blended for phonemic awareness practice.</li>
                        <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; margin-top: 4px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "The yellow ____ is bright." (sun) - Teacher emphasizes /s/ /ʌ/ /n/.</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example: "I see a pretty ______." (flower) - Teacher emphasizes /f/ /l/ /ɑʊ/ /ɚ/.</li>
                        </ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Pair Interaction (Peer Check and Read Aloud):</b> Students work in pairs to check their answers from the previous activities. They take turns reading one completed sentence each, focusing on clear pronunciation of the target vocabulary and sounds (/k/, /s/).</li>
                        <ul style="list-style-type: lower-alpha; margin-top: 4px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Partner A: "The sun is bright." Partner B: "I can see a big tree."</li>
                        </ul>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-17 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher provides a new, very short nature-themed text (similar to "My Happy Park Day" but with slight variations or a different focus on nature items). This text also includes a simple instruction to draw something.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Task Format:</b> Summarizing a nature text using a graphic organizer and following simple written drawing instructions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. Students receive a worksheet with a short text (e.g., "A Walk in Nature") and a simple graphic organizer (e.g., a box titled "Nature Words" and space for a drawing).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Text Example:</b> "A Walk in Nature. I walk on a trail. I can see a beautiful river. There are green leaves on the ground. A little bird is in the sky. I smell the flowers. It is quiet. I'm happy here. Draw a green leaf!"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. Students read the text independently.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. They identify 3-4 key nature terms (e.g., river, leaves, bird, flowers) from the text and write them in the "Nature Words" graphic organizer.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">4. Students then read and follow the written instruction at the end of the text (e.g., "Draw a green leaf!") by drawing it in the designated space on the worksheet.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">5. Students can briefly share their graphic organizer and drawing with a partner, pointing to the words they wrote and their drawing.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher observation during pair work, collection and review of student worksheets (graphic organizer and drawing).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their completed worksheet with the "Nature Words" graphic organizer and their drawing based on the text from Stage 4.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Identifies at least 3 key nature terms from the text for the graphic organizer. (Reading: Summarize)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Successfully follows the written drawing instruction (e.g., draws a leaf). (Reading: Follow instructions)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses legible handwriting for the words in the graphic organizer.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Attempts to pronounce words correctly during peer check (if observed).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete one of the following by circling Yes/No or drawing a happy/sad face:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. I can find nature words in a story. (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. I can draw what the story tells me. (Yes/No)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. What was easy to read in the nature stories today?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. What new nature word did you learn or practice today?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What reading comprehension strategies worked best for summarizing the text and following instructions? Were the graphic organizers effective for A1.1 students?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Were students able to identify and blend phonemes like /s/ in "sun" and /f/ /l/ /ɑʊ/ /ɚ/ in "flower" during practice? What adjustments or additional scaffolding (e.g., more picture support, simpler sentences) might be needed for the next reading lesson, or for supporting struggling readers?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b style="color: #1a5276;">Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">"Great job reading about nature! Next lesson, we will talk about our favorite nature places and what we can do there. We will use the words we read today to speak about our experiences outside."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>